{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tragedy of the Commons.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tragedy of the Commons.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tragedy of the commons tragedy of the commons","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tragedy of the Commons.md","fileName":"Tragedy of the Commons.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Tragedy of the Commons","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[System Dynamics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["System Dynamics","Resource","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tragedy of the Commons.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tragedy of the Commons.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tragedy of the commons tragedy of the commons","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tragedy of the Commons.md","fileName":"Tragedy of the Commons.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Tragedy of the Commons","heading":"Tragedy of the Commons","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The tragedy of the commons is a system pattern in which individuals acting in their own short-term interest deplete a limited shared resource. Each actor receives a concentrated benefit while the cost is distributed across the group.\n\nThe pattern can create conflict and strategic play when the shared [[Resource]] and its depletion are legible. Without meaningful coordination or balancing mechanisms, the common stock can collapse even though no participant intended that collective outcome.","tags":["baby"],"links":["System Dynamics","Resource","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tragedy of the Commons.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tragedy of the Commons.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tragedy of the